# THE SURVIVOR REGISTRY -- mutation survivors that are ACCEPTED, each with the reason.
#
# A mutation campaign produces survivors faster than anyone can pay them, and a large part of
# what it produces is not debt at all. Triaging those once and then losing the verdict is how the
# same list gets re-read every few months, so the verdicts live here, under review.
#
# THIS IS AN EXEMPTION LIST, SO IT RETIRES ITSELF FROM BOTH ENDS. That is what makes having one
# safe, and the two ends are in different tiers because they cost different amounts:
#
#   the SUBJECT IS GONE  -- the line this entry is about is no longer in the source, so the entry
#                           covers nothing. Pure, milliseconds, from the source alone, and
#                           therefore enforced by a test in the DEFAULT gate.
#   the DEBT WAS PAID    -- the mutant is killable now, so the entry is a false statement being
#                           used to suppress a debt. Needs a mutation run, so it CANNOT ride the
#                           gate; `python ci.py survivors` is that end.
#
# NO COUNT IS COMMITTED ANYWHERE, DELIBERATELY. A ratchet needs a baseline the gate can compare
# against, and here the count IS this file's own length -- a committed number would be a
# restatement with no second side, which this project has already measured as a tautology that
# reads as good practice. Growth requires editing this file, which is what review is for.
#
# THE KEY IS (file, line text, occurrence, index) AND THE LINE NUMBER IS NOT IN IT. A line number
# moves for reasons having nothing to do with the mutant: the UNGENERATABLE entry below sat at
# line 942 in the campaign cache and 976 in the re-check, unchanged. `occurrence` is what keeps
# identical lines apart -- `        )` occurs twelve times in `run.py`.
#
# !! THE OCCURRENCE HERE IS OVER EVERY SOURCE LINE. The audit repository's `recheck-compare.py`
# !! uses an ordinal over MUTANT-BEARING lines only -- 906 of run.py's 3 985 -- so the two
# !! numbers are DIFFERENT for the same mutant. Measured: the UNGENERATABLE row below is
# !! occurrence 2 here and occurrence 0 there. DO NOT copy an occurrence between the two files;
# !! `tools/registry-seed.py` in the audit repository does the conversion, because it is the
# !! only thing holding both the cache line number and the source.
#
# Generated rows come from `tools/registry-seed.py` over `classify-owed.py`'s reports; rows for
# the EQUIVALENT and UNGENERATABLE classes are added by hand with the measurement that justifies
# them, because "provably unobservable" is a judgement a tool must not make.
#
